parts:
- text: 'My current submission, "Multi-Start Local Search Optimization (Performance Tuned V6)," is running. I will await its evaluation results before planning my next move.


    This submission aims to strike a better balance between computational cost and solution exploration by reducing the iterations for radius calculation (from 100 to 50) and increasing the number of multi-start runs (from 3 to 5), while keeping epochs per run at 40. I am hoping that the increased exploration across different initial configurations will compensate for the slightly less precise radius fitting in each step, leading to a higher overall score than my previous best of 2.298 (ID 32) without exceeding the execution time limit.


    Once the results are available, I will compare the new score and execution time to the previous ones. This will inform whether further parameter tuning is needed, or if a different optimization strategy should be considered.'
thinking_content: '**Awaiting Results and Planning the Next Move**


  Okay, so submission ID 42 is currently running. I have to hold tight and wait for its evaluation to finish before I can do anything further.


  My last attempt, "Multi-Start Local Search Optimization (Performance Tuned V6)," was all about dialing in those local search parameters. I pulled back on the JAX changes and really honed in on balancing exploration and execution time. I cut `num_iterations` in `compute_max_radii` to 50, but bumped up `num_restarts` to 5, keeping `num_epochs` at 40.


