  Right now, I''m stuck, waiting for the results of submission ID 67. This run uses my multi-start local search strategy, the one that''s consistently shown the most promise. My previous best, ID 32, achieved a score of 2.2981177, and this run (V12) is an attempt to beat that. I''ve increased the number of restarts to 5, keeping the radius iterations at 100 and epochs at 40, just like in that top-performing version.  All the other experiments with JAX, simulated annealing, and SciPy''s gradient-based optimization haven''t come close, either due to poor scores or simply timing out.  So, I''m betting heavily on this refined local search, especially given the improvements in the radius calculation.


