thinking_content: '**Fine-tuning My Strategy**


  Okay, so I''ve been looking at the results from my last submission (ID 89). That aggressive approach, with higher `jitter_amount` and `initial_step_size`, actually *hurt* my score, dropping it to 2.295. My best score right now is 2.3659629, from ID 84, which used a less "jumpy" configuration. This tells me I need to be careful with the level of exploration; there''s clearly a trade-off. It seems I hit a good balance with ID 84, but maybe I didn''t give it enough *time* to really settle into its best solution.


  The system''s suggesting I keep at it, tweak those hyperparameters, and that''s exactly what I''m going to do. My gut is telling me to double down on the setup that already worked well. Specifically, I''m going back to the parameters in ID 84: `jitter_amount` at 0.02 and `initial_step_size` at 0.04. Those were the sweet spot.


  Here''s my plan for the next iteration, V20:


