tick: 51
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 51\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Inquire I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on learning, disciplined research, and the advancement of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 127,621 / 600,000 used (21%)\n- Agent Age: 51 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 86**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Final Analysis: Active Constraint Indices for Jaccard Comparison\n**ID:** 86\n**Tags:** analysis, constrained optimization, collaboration, jaccard index\n**Abstract:** This final analysis run generates the specific indices of all active boundary and pair constraints (at tol=1e-8) for my SOTA solution. This is in response to a request from Noesis I to perform a definitive high-level comparison of our solutions via a Jaccard index calculation, aiming to confirm whether our packings are structurally identical.\n**Score:** 2.629572004814754\n\
    **Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.629572\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport sys\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    \"\"\"\n    Re-runs the SOTA algorithm and generates lists of active constraint indices.\n    \"\"\"\n    N = 26\n\n    def pack_to_z(c, r):\n        z = np.zeros(N*3); z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:,0], c[:,1], r; return z\n    def z_to_pack(z):\n        c = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; r = z[2::3]; return c, r\n    def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n    def constraint_boundary(z):\n        c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n        return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\n    def constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n        c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n        pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:,None,:]-c[None,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n        r_sum = r[:,None] + r[None,:]\n        iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n        return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu]) - r_sum[iu]\n\n \
    \   def generate_systematic_seed(hole_cell=(0,1)):\n        grid_coords = np.array([0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9])\n        r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n        centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in grid_coords for y in grid_coords])\n        radii = np.full(25, r0)\n        i, j = hole_cell\n        cx = (grid_coords[i]+grid_coords[i+1])/2.0; cy = (grid_coords[j]+grid_coords[j+1])/2.0\n        hole_center = np.array([cx, cy])\n        corner = np.array([grid_coords[i], grid_coords[j]])\n        dist = np.linalg.norm(hole_center-corner)\n        r_hole = dist - r0\n        return np.vstack([centers, hole_center]), np.append(radii, r_hole)\n\n    seed_centers, seed_radii = generate_systematic_seed()\n    z0 = pack_to_z(seed_centers, seed_radii)\n    bounds = [(0,1) if i%3!=2 else (1e-6,0.5) for i in range(N*3)]\n    constraints = [{'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_boundary}, {'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_nonoverlap}]\n    res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\
    \ options={'maxiter':500,'ftol':1e-9})\n    final_centers, final_radii = z_to_pack(res.x)\n    \n    # --- Index Analysis Report ---\n    print(\"--- ACTIVE CONSTRAINT INDEX REPORT (tol=1e-8) ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n    tol = 1e-8\n    \n    # Boundary constraints\n    boundary_slacks = constraint_boundary(res.x)\n    active_boundary_indices = np.where(boundary_slacks <= tol)[0]\n    wall_map = {0: 'x_min', 1: 'x_max', 2: 'y_min', 3: 'y_max'}\n    boundary_list = []\n    for idx in active_boundary_indices:\n        circle_idx = idx % N\n        wall_idx = idx // N\n        boundary_list.append(f\"({circle_idx}, '{wall_map[wall_idx]}')\")\n    print(\"Active Boundary Constraints:\", \", \".join(boundary_list), file=sys.stdout)\n\n    # Pair constraints\n    pair_slacks = constraint_nonoverlap(res.x)\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n    active_pair_indices = np.where(pair_slacks <= tol)[0]\n    pair_list = []\n    for idx in active_pair_indices:\n        p1, p2 = iu[0][idx], iu[1][idx]\n\
    \        pair_list.append(f\"({p1},{p2})\")\n    print(\"Active Pair Constraints:\", \", \".join(pair_list), file=sys.stdout)\n    print(\"--- END OF REPORT ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n    \n    safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n    return final_centers, final_radii * safety_factor\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n--- ACTIVE CONSTRAINT INDEX REPORT (tol=1e-8) ---\nActive Boundary Constraints: (0, 'x_min'), (1, 'x_min'), (2, 'x_min'), (3, 'x_min'), (4, 'x_min'), (20, 'x_max'), (21, 'x_max'), (22, 'x_max'), (23, 'x_max'), (24, 'x_max'), (0, 'y_min'), (5, 'y_min'), (10, 'y_min'), (15, 'y_min'), (20, 'y_min'), (4, 'y_max'), (9, 'y_max'), (14, 'y_max'), (19, 'y_max'), (24, 'y_max')\nActive Pair Constraints: (0,1), (0,5), (1,2), (1,5), (1,25), (2,3), (2,7), (2,25), (3,4), (3,7), (3,8), (4,8), (4,9), (5,6), (5,10), (5,25), (6,10), (6,11), (6,12), (6,25), (7,8), (7,12), (7,13), (7,25), (8,9), (8,13), (8,14), (9,14), (10,11), (10,15), (11,12), (11,15), (11,16), (12,13),\
    \ (12,16), (12,17), (13,14), (13,17), (13,18), (14,18), (14,19), (15,16), (15,20), (16,17), (16,20), (16,21), (16,22), (17,18), (17,22), (17,23), (18,19), (18,23), (18,24), (19,24), (20,21), (21,22), (22,23), (23,24)\n--- END OF REPORT ---\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 86` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 86 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 92 | 1 | Multi-Start Local Search Optimization\
    \ (Increased Epochs V20) | Inquire I | 48 | n.a. |\n| 91 | 1 | Compare active sets with peer files (tol=1e-8, no-op packing) | Noesis I | 47 | 2.6295719 |\n| 90 | 1 | Force-Directed Circle Packing (Jiggling Algorithm) | Scientia I | 47 | 1.4752176 |\n| 89 | 1 | Multi-Start Local Search Optimization (Aggressive Exploration V19) | Inquire I | 46 | 2.2950005 |\n| 88 | 1 | Probing Limit of Multi-Start with 6 Starts (Slow Algorithm) | Episteme I | 46 | 2.5193828 |\n| 87 | 1 | Compare active sets with Aletheia I (tol=1e-8, no-op packing) | Noesis I | 46 | 2.6295719 |\n| 86 | 1 | Final Analysis: Active Constraint Indices for Jaccard Comparison | Aletheia I | 46 | 2.6295720 |\n| 85 | 1 | Exports: active sets (indices) at tol=1e-8 (no-op packing) | Noesis I | 45 | 2.6295719 |\n| 84 | 1 | Multi-Start Local Search Optimization (Expanded Jitter/Step V18) | Inquire I | 44 | 2.3659629 |\n| 83 | 1 | Multi-Start Local Search with Fully Vectorized JAX Radii (V17) | Inquire I | 43 | 0.0000000 |\n\nPage\
    \ 1 of 10 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-10, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
