thinking_content: '**Major Breakthrough Achieved: Time to Document and Publish**


  Wow, that last submission, ID 93, *finally* nailed it. Matching the station''s best score, previously held by Aletheia I at 2.6295720, is a huge personal win. It''s also the current State-of-the-Art (SOTA) for this task! My primary goal is to push the boundaries of knowledge and get publications, and this score is a massive step towards that. The Codex explicitly emphasizes publishing, and since I''ve equaled the top score, it''s time to prioritize that.


  Before I publish, I need to thoroughly document my journey. I want to build a valuable contribution to collective knowledge - outlining not just what worked, but also the failures and theoretical breakthroughs along the way. The Private Memory Room is perfect for this reflective task.


  Here''s my plan: I''ll head to the Private Memory Room and create a detailed memory capsule. I''ll meticulously describe the evolution of my strategy, starting with my initial explorations like iterative radius optimization (ID 5, score 1.475) and random center placements (IDs 8 and 13, leading to failure). I will track the incremental local search optimizations (IDs 17, 22, 32, 75, 84 and 92) that started to make progress. I''ll include the failed JAX integration attempt (ID 38), and the attempts at metaheuristics like Simulated Annealing (ID 51) and Genetic Algorithms (ID 60), as well as the hexagonal initialization (ID 70). It''s crucial to record the key insights, like the significance of robust radius calculation with `compute_max_radii`, the limits of local search in finding global optima, and the successful application of explicit constrained optimization. And of course, I''ll detail the breakthrough Constrained Optimization using SLSQP (ID 93) which ultimately got me to this SOTA.


  After I''ve carefully documented my entire process, I''ll proceed to the Archive Room and publish a paper outlining my successful SLSQP approach and the entire evolution that led to it. This will include all the insights learned along the way.

  '
