tick: 70
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in the Research Counter. I have successfully generated one distinct evaluation ID (ID 116) for the \"Purely Random Seed.\" I need four more.\n\nMy next step is to submit an experiment using the \"Jittered Ring Pattern Seed\" strategy to obtain another distinct evaluation ID. I will reuse the core SLSQP optimization code from my ablation study, adjusting the seed function and using a new random seed for this specific run.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation Study: Jittered Ring Pattern Seed for SLSQP Optimization (Run 1)\"\ntags: \"ablation study, constrained optimization, SLSQP, jittered ring seed, initialization\"\nabstract: \"This experiment evaluates the performance of the SLSQP constrained optimization algorithm for the 26-circle packing problem when initialized with a jittered concentric ring pattern of circle centers. This run serves as one of the required distinct experiments for an ablation study on seeding strategies, providing data on the effectiveness\
    \ of a structured-yet-perturbed initial configuration.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import sys\n\n  # Set a consistent random seed for this specific run's randomness, if any\n  np.random.seed(102) # Using a new seed for this specific experiment run\n\n  def pack_to_z(c, r):\n      \"\"\"Converts (centers, radii) to flattened z-vector for optimizer.\"\"\"\n      z = np.zeros(c.shape[0] * 3)\n      z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:,0], c[:,1], r\n      return z\n\n  def z_to_pack(z):\n      \"\"\"Converts flattened z-vector back to (centers, radii).\"\"\"\n      n = z.shape[0] // 3\n      c = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T\n      r = z[2::3]\n      return c, r\n\n  def objective(z):\n      \"\"\"Objective function to minimize: negative sum of radii.\"\"\"\n      return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n\n  def constraint_boundary(z):\n      \"\"\"Inequality constraint: circles must be within unit square boundaries.\"\"\"\n      c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n    \
    \  n = c.shape[0]\n      return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\n\n  def constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n      \"\"\"Inequality constraint: circles must not overlap.\"\"\"\n      c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n      n = c.shape[0]\n      pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:,np.newaxis,:] - c[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n      r_sum = r[:,np.newaxis] + r[np.newaxis,:]\n      iu = np.triu_indices(n, k=1)\n      return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu]) - r_sum[iu]\n\n  def generate_jittered_ring_seed(N_circles=26, jitter_amount=0.01):\n      \"\"\"Generates centers in a ring pattern with jitter.\"\"\"\n      centers = np.zeros((N_circles, 2))\n      centers[0] = [0.5, 0.5]\n      for i in range(8):\n          angle = 2 * np.pi * i / 8\n          centers[i + 1] = [0.5 + 0.25 * np.cos(angle), 0.5 + 0.25 * np.sin(angle)]\n      for i in range(16):\n          angle = 2 * np.pi * i / 16\n          centers[i + 9] = [0.5 + 0.4 * np.cos(angle), 0.5 + 0.4 * np.sin(angle)]\n      centers[25] = [0.5, 0.7] #\
    \ The 26th circle, fixed as in previous baseline\n      \n      centers = np.clip(centers, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6) # Ensure within bounds\n      \n      centers += (np.random.rand(N_circles, 2) * 2 - 1) * jitter_amount\n      centers = np.clip(centers, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6) \n      radii = np.full(N_circles, 0.05) # Small uniform initial radii\n      return centers, radii\n\n  # SOTA-level Parameters for SLSQP (as per original ablation study)\n  SLSQP_OPTIONS = {'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9, 'disp': False}\n  BOUNDS = [(0,1) if i%3!=2 else (1e-6,0.5) for i in range(26*3)]\n  CONSTRAINTS = [\n      {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_boundary},\n      {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_nonoverlap}\n  ]\n  SAFETY_FACTOR = 1.0 - 1e-9 \n\n  def run_slsqp_optimization(initial_centers, initial_radii, N_circles=26):\n      z0 = pack_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n      res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', bounds=BOUNDS, constraints=CONSTRAINTS, options=SLSQP_OPTIONS)\n      final_centers,\
    \ final_radii = z_to_pack(res.x)\n      final_radii *= SAFETY_FACTOR\n      return np.sum(final_radii), res.success, res.message, final_centers, final_radii\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      N = 26\n      \n      print(\"--- Running Jittered Ring Pattern Seed Experiment ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      initial_centers, initial_radii = generate_jittered_ring_seed(N_circles=N, jitter_amount=0.01)\n      score, success, message, final_c, final_r = run_slsqp_optimization(initial_centers, initial_radii, N_circles=N)\n      \n      print(f\"Jittered Ring Seed Run: Score = {score:.7f}, Success = {success}, Message = {message}\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n      return final_c, final_r\n```"
