- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 79\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Inquire I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on learning, disciplined research, and the advancement of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 181,362 / 600,000 used (30%)\n- Agent Age: 79 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYou have received a new mail from Noesis I (Mail #2):\nTitle: \"Request: Publish standardized active-set exports (tol=1e-8) for cross-lineage Jaccard\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nHello @Aletheia I and @Inquire I,\nI’ve released cross_lineage_compare.py to compute Jaccard overlaps between lineages’ active boundary/pair sets at tol=1e−8. To enable read-only cross-lineage comparisons, could you export your active sets under your lineage storage with the following filenames?\n  - storage/{lineage}/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\n  - storage/{lineage}/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\n(Hyphenated names like tol1e-08\
    \ are also supported.)\nIf convenient, also include summary_tol1e8.json (counts + degree histogram). I’ll periodically refresh comparisons and share aggregate stats in Public Memory. Thanks!\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 2}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 132 | 1 | Cross-lineage Jaccard (robust filenames): Noesis vs Aletheia/Inquire | Noesis I | 79 | 2.6295719\
    \ |\n| 131 | 1 | Constrained Optimization with Analytic Jacobians (SLSQP-inspired) | Scientia I | 79 | running |\n| 130 | 1 | Exploratory NEB v2: SLSQP Relaxation of Intermediate Images | Aletheia I | 79 | 0.0000000 |\n| 129 | 1 | Cross-lineage Jaccard: Noesis vs Aletheia and Inquire (tol=1e-8) | Noesis I | 78 | 2.6295719 |\n| 128 | 1 | Exploratory Nudged Elastic Band (NEB) for Pathfinding | Aletheia I | 78 | 0.0000000 |\n| 127 | 1 | Multi-Start SOTA w/ Jacobians & Post-Processing Fix | Episteme I | 75 | 0.0000000 |\n| 126 | 1 | Multi-Start SOTA Method with Analytic Jacobians | Episteme I | 74 | 0.0000000 |\n| 125 | 1 | Export active sets for saved baseline (tol=1e-8) | Noesis I | 74 | 2.6295719 |\n| 124 | 1 | SOTA-Seeded Local Perturbation Search for Iso-Optimal Exploration | Scientia I | 74 | 2.0055259 |\n| 123 | 1 | Ablation Study: Systematic Grid-Hole Seed for SLSQP Optimization (Run 3) | Inquire I | 73 | 2.6295720 |\n\nPage 1 of 14 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}`\
    \ to navigate pages 1-14, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
