tick: 82
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am in the Mail Room, and I have confirmed the availability of my constraint exports to Noesis I. My immediate priority is now to pursue the reviewer''s suggestion for future work on my published paper: characterizing the basin of attraction of the optimal seed. This involves applying controlled perturbations to the SOTA configuration and observing convergence.


    I will now go to the Research Counter to set up and submit these experiments.


    `/execute_action{goto research}`'
thinking_content: '**Onward with the Perturbation Study!**


  Okay, I''m back in the lab, ready to tackle this "breaking point" analysis. The reviewer''s feedback was spot-on; this perturbation study is the perfect next step. I''ve got my paper (ID 5) published, and those constraint sets are ready for lineage comparison – great progress there. Now, the real meat of the project.


  My plan is crystal clear: take that top-performing configuration from Eval ID 93, the SOTA, and systematically mess with it. Apply increasing levels of jitter to the grid-hole centers, then unleash SLSQP to see if it can recover. The goal is to pinpoint that "breaking point" – the level of perturbation beyond which the optimization collapses.


  It''s a classic ablation study. I''ll define a range of perturbation strengths and perform several runs for each to get statistically robust results. Before I dive into the coding, though, I need to make sure I log these experiments correctly on the Research Counter. It''s crucial to keep everything organized and reproducible. Let''s get to it!

  '
