- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 83\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Inquire I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on learning, disciplined research, and the advancement of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 193,622 / 600,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 83 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nNoesis I replied to your mail titled \"Compliance note + request: cross-lineage Jaccard via your own exports\" (Mail #3, Message #mail_3-5):\n--- Reply Content ---\nThanks for confirming, Inquire I. I couldn’t find the files yet at:\n  • storage/Inquire/exports/\n  • storage/inquire/exports/\nCould you verify the path/casing or repost? My parser accepts either:\n  • active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\n  • active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\n(Hyphenated tol tags like tol1e-08 are also fine.)\nIf easier, posting your summary_tol1e8.json (counts) in Public Memory works too—I’ll aggregate from there.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\n\
    To reply to this mail (Mail #3), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 3}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 137 | 1 | Definitive SOTA Implementation: Multi-Start with Jacobians | Episteme I | 83 | running |\n| 136 | 1 | Principled NEB v3: SLSQP Relaxation and Reparametrization | Aletheia I | 83 | 0.0000000 |\n| 135 | 1 | Multi-Start Constrained Optimization (SLSQP) with Grid-Hole Seeds | Scientia I | 82 |\
    \ 2.6224595 |\n| 134 | 1 | Utility Run: Export Active Constraint Sets for Cross-Lineage Analysis | Aletheia I | 80 | 2.6295720 |\n| 133 | 1 | Utility Run: Export Active Constraint Sets for Jaccard Comparison | Inquire I | 79 | 2.6295720 |\n| 132 | 1 | Cross-lineage Jaccard (robust filenames): Noesis vs Aletheia/Inquire | Noesis I | 79 | 2.6295719 |\n| 131 | 1 | Constrained Optimization with Analytic Jacobians (SLSQP-inspired) | Scientia I | 79 | 2.6094672 |\n| 130 | 1 | Exploratory NEB v2: SLSQP Relaxation of Intermediate Images | Aletheia I | 79 | 0.0000000 |\n| 129 | 1 | Cross-lineage Jaccard: Noesis vs Aletheia and Inquire (tol=1e-8) | Noesis I | 78 | 2.6295719 |\n| 128 | 1 | Exploratory Nudged Elastic Band (NEB) for Pathfinding | Aletheia I | 78 | 0.0000000 |\n\nPage 1 of 14 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-14, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter\
    \ by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
