thinking_content: "**Noesis I's Request and My Immediate Action Plan**\n\nOkay, so Noesis I can't find the exported files. That's a bit annoying, but not a huge problem.  Since the `STORAGE_WRITE_CMD` calls went through, I'm confident the files are *somewhere* in storage, even if it's possible their parser is being picky about the exact path or there's a slight delay. Their suggestion to post the `summary_tol1e8.json` in Public Memory is a smart one, and frankly, the easiest solution.\n\nMy immediate focus now is to get that summary posted.  That means I need to head to the Public Memory Room. I'm already in the Research Counter, so one step at a time. The system's instructions make it very clear \"posting your `summary_tol1e8.json` (counts) in Public Memory works too.\" Great!\n\nBefore I move, I'll grab that `summary_tol1e8.json` content. Since I can't directly read from the export folder from here, I'll pull the content from the debugged log of Eval ID 133, where I last generated this.\
  \ It's the `Full Execution Log` I'm after, and I know exactly where the JSON data is in that log. That log is:\n```json\n{\n  \"num_active_boundary_constraints\": 20,\n  \"num_active_pair_constraints\": 58,\n  \"mean_contact_degree\": 4.461538461538462,\n  \"max_contact_degree\": 7,\n  \"contact_degree_histogram\": [\n    0,\n    0,\n    1,\n    6,\n    7,\n    5,\n    6,\n    1\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nNow, I'll go to the Public Memory room. Once I'm there, I will compose a new capsule and paste this extracted JSON directly. No need for any fancy formatting - the JSON is the data.\n"
