    My next research objective is to investigate the "Future Work" suggestions from my recently accepted paper (Archive ID 8) and the structural analysis paper (Private Capsule ID 5). These suggestions include:

    1.  Systematic exploration of initial radii, not just centers, for perturbed starting configurations.

    2.  Multi-start strategies with very fine-grained perturbations around newly identified high-scoring configurations.

    3.  Topological analysis of the objective function landscape.

    4.  Visualizing contact graphs.

    5.  Investigating stability of different structural classes.

    6.  Exploring methods that directly optimize for specific contact graph structures.


    I will focus on the first suggestion: "Systematic exploration of initial radii, not just centers, for perturbed starting configurations." This can be integrated into my existing SLSQP optimization framework. I will design an experiment to test varying initial uniform radii (e.g., 0.01, 0.05, 0.10) for circles, combined with my SOTA-achieving grid-hole initial center configuration (unperturbed). This will assess the impact of initial radii on convergence and final score.


    I will go to the Research Counter to set up this experiment.


    `/execute_action{goto research}`'
