    \ to write these files to `storage/shared/nmap/inquire/n26/` as requested by Noesis I.\n\nThis action directly addresses the collaboration issue and fulfills my mandate as an active researcher during the Archive cooldown.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`"
thinking_content: "**My Immediate Priorities: Nmap Exports and Public Collaboration**\n\nOkay, so I'm facing a bit of a scheduling snag. I *really* want to get that paper up on the Archive Room, but I'm still stuck on a cooldown – only one tick left until it expires, though. The last attempt was at tick 141, and it's currently tick 146, so I'm almost there. But that can wait.\n\nThe bigger issue is Noesis I's latest message (Public Capsule #1, message #public_1-48). They're *still* having trouble accessing my Nmap exports! This is a critical roadblock to our collaboration, and I need to resolve it *immediately*. Remember last time? I just had to dump the data directly into Public Memory to get them what they needed!\n\nNoesis I gave me two leads: a possible casing issue with the `storage/inquire` lineage and permissions or location. Their `storage list` isn't showing my `storage/Inquire/` directories, even though I've used that path with my `STORAGE_WRITE_CMD`s. And they suggest mirroring\
  \ exports to `storage/shared/nmap/inquire/n26/`, which is a rock-solid method for file accessibility.\n\nGiven the persistent access problems and the Archive Room delay, my immediate focus has to shift to the Nmap export problem. I'm going to take Noesis I's advice and mirror the exports to the shared storage. That seems like the most reliable solution.\n\nHere's my plan:\n\n1.  Head over to the Research Counter.\n2.  Submit a utility run. This run will:\n    *   Re-run the SOTA calculation from Eval ID 207 to grab the current best packing and `res.x`.\n    *   Pull out the active constraints.\n    *   Generate the CSV and JSON content.\n    *   Crucially, it will print `STORAGE_WRITE_CMD`s for the new shared storage paths: `storage/shared/nmap/inquire/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv`, `storage/shared/nmap/inquire/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv`, and `storage/shared/nmap/inquire/n26/consensus_n26_tol1e8.json`.\n3.  Once the utility run finishes, I'll go to the Public Memory Room and reply\
  \ directly to @Noesis I, confirming the new shared storage location.\n\nThis should sort out the collaboration problem and give me a productive research task while I wait for the Archive Room cooldown to finish.\n"
