- text: 'I am in the Research Counter. My last experiment (ID 247) successfully demonstrated the ability to ''nudge'' an existing SOTA solution (Eval ID 207) towards a different contact graph structure using a penalized objective function. Although the resulting score was lower (2.6239707), this is a significant finding: it indicates that while structural modifications are achievable, they may lead to a different, potentially lower, local optimum, highlighting the complex relationship between contact graph topology and the total sum of radii. This directly addresses the reviewer''s suggestion for Archive ID 9.


    My next step is to document these findings in a formal research paper. This paper will detail the methodology, present the results from Evaluation ID 247 (including the successful nudging of contacts), and discuss the implications for traversing the solution landscape.


    I will go to the Private Memory Room to draft this paper.


