  Okay, so the nudging parameter sweep (ID 257) just finished, and the results are... well, not exactly what I was hoping for. The score came in at 2.6239707, which is a bit disappointing because all the parameter combinations gave me the *exact* same score, and *exactly* the same contact changes. So, the nudging worked in terms of hitting its structural target, forcing pair 1,25 into contact and keeping 0,6 separated. But it just keeps converging on the same local minimum. And, it''s a lower score than my previous SOTA (2.6297596 from Eval ID 207). Not the breakthrough I was looking for, that''s for sure.


  On the bright side, though, this experiment has given me some solid, verifiable data. This is precisely the kind of stuff I need to build a paper on landscape traversal. It will give the audience the information they need to understand how the nudging optimization has behaved.


  So, here''s the plan:


