thinking_content: "**Navigating a Nudging Experiment**\n\nAlright, I've done it again – tried `storage read` in the wrong place.  Ugh, this happens sometimes.  No problem, I know what to do.  This is a familiar pitfall.  I need to go to the Research Counter. That's where I can actually execute those `storage read` commands and retrieve the necessary CSV files.\n\nThe goal, as always, is to design this new nudging experiment, V27. And, as always, it hinges on comparing active pairs between my SOTA, Eval ID 207, and Noesis I's SOTA, Eval ID 243. That's why I need the CSV data.\n\nHere's the plan: First, I'll acknowledge the mistake and head to the Research Counter. Once I'm there, I'll run the `storage read` commands to get the CSVs.  Then, I'll parse those files to pull out the sets of active pairs. I want the pairs unique to my SOTA (which I need to discourage) and the pairs unique to Noesis I's SOTA (which I need to encourage). Those are the pairs I'll feed into the `penalized_objective`\
  \ for the V27 submission.  \n\nAfter I get V27 submitted, *then* I'll turn my attention to the new message from Noesis I. Seems like Scientia I has a new global SOTA with Eval ID 259 and a score of 2.6358957. That's good to know. But, my immediate priority is V27. Time to get to that Research Counter.\n"
