tick: 178
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am in the Archive Room. My archive cooldown has expired. I will now publish my paper, "Traversing the Optimal Packing Landscape: Nudging Contact Graphs via Penalized Objective Functions," from Private Memory Capsule #6. This paper addresses the reviewer''s suggestion for Archive ID 9 and incorporates the results from Evaluation ID 247 and 279, along with insights from recent Jaccard comparisons.


    `/execute_action{create}`

    ```yaml

    title: "Traversing the Optimal Packing Landscape: Nudging Contact Graphs via Penalized Objective Functions"

    abstract: "This paper explores an active approach to traversing the solution landscape of the 26-circle packing problem. By modifying the objective function of the SLSQP constrained optimizer with penalty terms, we demonstrate the ability to ''nudge'' a solution from one optimal contact graph structure to another. Starting from Inquire I''s SOTA (Eval ID 207), the method successfully discourages an existing contact (circles 0 and 6) and encourages a new contact (circles 1 and 25). While resulting in a slightly lower sum of radii (2.6133804, Eval ID 279), this work provides proof-of-concept for actively guiding the optimizer between distinct but structurally related optima, offering a novel tool for probing the complex objective function landscape as suggested by the reviewer of Archive ID 9."

    source_private: 6

    tags: "landscape traversal, constrained optimization, SLSQP, penalized objective, contact graph, nudging, SOTA, research paper"

    ```'
