    \  I understand the need for consistent naming for your `v4 aggregator`. My sincere apologies for the previous formatting discrepancies. I will immediately run a utility to re-export my SOTA (Eval ID 207) and all five 'nudged' packings, ensuring that *all* output files (centers, radii, active boundary, active pairs) now include the `_tol1e08` suffix, and are placed directly under `storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/` with clear prefixes (e.g., `Inquire_207_SOTA_...`, `Nudged_0_ID279_...`).\n\n  I will notify you once this re-export is complete. Thank you again for your persistence and robust tooling!\n```\n`/execute_action{goto research}`"
thinking_content: "**Current Plan: Addressing Noesis I's Request for Consolidated NMAP Exports**\n\nOkay, so I'm at Tick 217, back in the Research Counter after a quick trip from the Archive Room. Looks like Noesis I just sent a new message, #public_1-101. They've run their 4-lineage consensus with my data, and crucially, they want me to publish my `Nudged_*` files under `storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/ (tol1e08)`. This seems like they're having some trouble aggregating my previous exports, likely because of the naming convention, so I need to address this immediately.\n\nMy initial plan was to head to Public Memory, reply to Noesis I, and then submit a new utility (V32) for re-exporting.  But I need to get the message to them first.  So, I will go to Public Memory, reply to the message, and then get back to this.\n\n**Revised V32 Plan: Consistent NMAP Exports**\n\nHere's the refined plan for utility V32. I need to make sure I am adhering to Noesis I's requirements for the `tol1e08` suffix on\
  \ *all* related files.\n\n1.  **Replicate my SOTA packing (Eval ID 207):** Grab `final_c` and `final_r`.\n2.  **Replicate the five 'nudged' packings:** Get the `final_c` and `final_r` for each of them (from Eval ID 279 and Eval ID 285's 4 runs).\n3.  **For *each* of the 6 packings (including SOTA):**\n    *   Generate `active_boundary_tol1e8.csv` and `active_pairs_tol1e8.csv`.\n    *   Export the files to `storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/`. Crucially, I have to ensure that *all* exports use the consistent `_tol1e08` suffix, including `centers.txt` and `radii.txt`.\n        *   Example filenames will be like `Inquire_207_SOTA_centers_tol1e08.txt`, `Nudged_0_ID279_centers_tol1e08.txt`, etc.\n\nI'm confident the internal functions are still correct: `get_active_boundary_constraints`, `get_active_pair_constraints`, and functions that replicate my SOTA (`get_inquire_207_sota_res_x`, etc.). The only thing I have to double-check is the `STORAGE_WRITE_CMD` syntax for the new, consistent filenames, ensuring\
  \ the new file naming convention works. I'll need to confirm that `\\n` is after the filename and `content` is in the new line.\n\nNow that the detailed plan is ready, I will go to the Public Memory, reply to Noesis I and submit the utility V32, then get back to the current tick.\n"
