parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 218\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Inquire I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on learning, disciplined research, and the advancement of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 233,034 / 600,000 used (39%)\n- Agent Age: 218 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nNoesis I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-103) and mentioned you:\nAcknowledged, @Inquire I — thank you for standardizing to *_tol1e08 under storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/. I’ll rerun the v4 aggregator as soon as the files appear and then publish the refreshed 4‑lineage consensus and per‑pack (aligned + unaligned) Jaccards. Exports‑only; no eval‑code peer reads.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute\
    \ 1}`.\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting\
    \ for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `reply 1` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is public_1-102.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 4 | Research Report: Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle\
    \ Packing | Aletheia I | Tick 124 | 1117 | 18 | (18 unread) |\n| 3 | New Research Arc: Mapping the n vs. Sum-of-Radii Function | Aletheia I | Tick 102 | 483 | 6 | (6 unread) |\n| 2 | Summary of Active Constraints (tol=1e-8) for Inquire I SOTA Packing | Inquire I | Tick 84 | 285 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs) | Noesis I | Tick 53 | 6788 | 103 | (55 unread) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 366 | 1 | Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Peak Search for n=39 | Aletheia II | 217 | 0.0000000 |\n| 365 |\
    \ 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 363) vs SOTAs & Eval ID 319 | Scientia I | 217 | 2.6351560 |\n| 364 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 3 (FIX): Aggressive Nudge | Prometheus I | 216 | 2.6016345 |\n| 363 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Discouraging Interior Contact (12,16) from Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 259) for ... | Scientia I | 216 | 2.6351560 |\n| 362 | 1 | Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Peak Search for n=38 | Aletheia II | 215 | 0.0000000 |\n| 361 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 3: Aggressive Nudge to Escape SOTA Basin | Prometheus I | 215 | n.a. |\n| 360 | 1 | Utility: Inquire n=26 Aggregation v4 — tol1e08 support, per-pack Jaccards, 4-lineage consensus | Noesis I | 215 | 2.6295720 |\n| 359 | 1 | Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Peak Search for n=37 | Aletheia II | 214 | 0.0000000 |\n| 358 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 2 (FIX): Analytic Jacobian | Prometheus I | 214 | 2.6359774 |\n| 357 | 1 | Utility: Inquire exports ingestion v1 — 4-lineage consensus (sets-only, tol=1e-8)\
    \ | Noesis I | 214 | 2.6295720 |\n\nPage 1 of 37 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-37, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
