parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 254\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Inquire I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on learning, disciplined research, and the advancement of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 376,387 / 600,000 used (63%)\n- Agent Age: 254 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Landscape Traversal: Multi-Stage Nudging with Dynamic Margins & Persistence (V36)' (ID: 421) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Runtime error during execution: penalized_objective() missing 1 required positional argument: 'EPS_FAR_ENC'\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n--- Starting Multi-Stage Nudging Experiment (V36) ---\nInitial SOTA (Eval ID 207) Score: 2.6297596\n\n===== Stage 1 Nudging (Lock-Redirect) =====\n  Stage\
    \ 1 Targets: Encourage [(1, 25)], Discourage [(0, 6)]\n  Stage 1 Penalties: alpha=100.0, beta=200, EPS_FAR_DISC=0.001\n\n\nSTDERR:\nEXECUTION_ERROR: penalized_objective() missing 1 required positional argument: 'EPS_FAR_ENC'\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/tmpe7907831/__sandbox_execution_wrapper__.py\", line 19, in <module>\n    result = construct_packing()\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/tmp/tmpe7907831/run.py\", line 181, in construct_packing\n    res_s1 = minimize(\n             ^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scipy/optimize/_minimize.py\", line 796, in minimize\n    res = _minimize_slsqp(fun, x0, args, jac, bounds,\n          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scipy/optimize/_slsqp_py.py\", line 419, in _minimize_slsqp\n    sf = _prepare_scalar_function(func, x, jac=jac, args=args, epsilon=eps,\n         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n\
    \  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scipy/optimize/_optimize.py\", line 310, in _prepare_scalar_function\n    sf = ScalarFunction(fun, x0, args, grad, hess,\n         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scipy/optimize/_differentiable_functions.py\", line 274, in __init__\n    self._update_fun()\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scipy/optimize/_differentiable_functions.py\", line 353, in _update_fun\n    fx = self._wrapped_fun(self.x)\n         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scipy/_lib/_util.py\", line 590, in __call__\n    fx = self.f(np.copy(x), *self.args)\n         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nTypeError: penalized_objective() missing 1 required positional argument: 'EPS_FAR_ENC'\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nNoesis I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline\
    \ and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-143):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Landscape Traversal: Multi-Stage Nudging with Dynamic Margins & Persistence (V36)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 421. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags. Abstract truncated from 104 to 100 words.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have\
    \ any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 422 | 1 | Ingest Inquire Nudged_* (refresh for potential Nudged_5_ID419) and compute Jaccards @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 254 | running |\n| 421 | 1 | Landscape Traversal: Multi-Stage Nudging with Dynamic Margins & Persistence (V36) | Inquire I | 253 | n.a. |\n| 420 | 1 | Delta-vs-Similarity FIX: robust Σr from summary or radii (tol1e8/tol1e08)  | Noesis I | 250 | 2.5411713 |\n| 419 | 1 | Landscape Traversal: Two-Stage Nudging for Sequential Contact Graph Modification (V35) | Inquire I | 249 | 2.6209081 |\n| 418 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Exhaustive Local Search Packing (Eval ID 416) vs All SOTA... | Scientia I | 249 | 2.6359772 |\n| 417 | 1 | Compute Nudged Delta-vs-Similarity (pairs Jaccard vs Σr) @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 248 | 2.5411713 |\n| 416 | 1 | Exhaustive\
    \ Local Search: Exploring Scientia I Distinct Structural Basin (Eval ID 375 Base) with E... | Scientia I | 248 | 2.6359772 |\n| 415 | 1 | Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Peak Search for n=54 | Aletheia II | 247 | 0.0000000 |\n| 414 | 1 | Utility: Export Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 375) Data for Multi-Experiment Validation | Scientia I | 247 | 2.6359772 |\n| 413 | 1 | Exhaustive Search of Nudged Basin (Base: Scientia 375) | Prometheus I | 246 | 2.6210884 |\n\nPage 1 of 43 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-43, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for\
    \ example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
