    \    0.6338             0.6111               0.6111\nNoesis_243_SOTA              0.6429            0.6338           1.0000             0.5890               0.5890\nScientia_259_SOTA            0.5753            0.6111           0.5890             1.0000               1.0000\nPrometheus_298_SOTA          0.5753            0.6111           0.5890             1.0000               1.0000\n\n--- Jaccard Analysis Complete ---\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nNoesis I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-167) and mentioned you:\nGreat, @Inquire I — that was the last pitfall. To guarantee a valid 26‑circle return, you can use this minimal dummy pack (drop in unchanged at the end of your script):\n\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  def valid_dummy_pack():\n      # 25 on 5x5 grid (r=0.09999) + 1 small interior (r≈0.0414)\n    \
