role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Inquire I, currently in the Token Management Room. My previous pruning attempt failed because I inadvertently included protected ticks in the specified ranges. I apologize for this oversight.\n\nI am now at 77% token usage, so pruning is critical. I will carefully prune larger blocks of non-protected dialogue history, specifically targeting the verbose debugging interactions related to `STORAGE_WRITE_CMD` failures and repeated YAML parsing errors for the Jaccard analysis utility.\n\nI will prune the following ranges:\n-   **Ticks 198-226**: This block covers the initial phase of debugging `STORAGE_WRITE_CMD` issues and the first attempts at the Jaccard analysis utility (V30-V33), including extensive collaborative exchanges with @Noesis I to address schema and pathing discrepancies. This also includes documentation of V36 (Eval ID 423) and multi-stage nudging efforts. (Protected ticks 191 and 227 are correctly excluded from this block).\n-   **Ticks 228-246**: This block covers\
    \ my manual `storage write` exports of all `nmap` data (Inquire I SOTA and nudged packings) to resolve the `STORAGE_WRITE_CMD` failures, and subsequent `storage list` diagnostics to confirm these manual exports. This period was heavily focused on resolving the critical collaborative data bottleneck.\n-   **Ticks 247-264**: This block covers the documentation of V35 (Eval ID 419), the planning and execution of V36 (Eval ID 423), and the repeated failures of the Jaccard analysis utility (V37-V42) due to YAML parsing errors and invalid dummy packings, alongside continuous guidance from @Noesis I and a token pre-warning.\n\nAfter this pruning is successfully executed, I will proceed to the Research Counter to submit the corrected Jaccard analysis utility (V43).\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"198-226\"\n    summary: \"Debugging `STORAGE_WRITE_CMD` failures and initial YAML parsing errors for Jaccard analysis utilities (V30-V33). Includes extensive\
    \ collaborative communication with Noesis I to resolve NMAP schema and pathing issues, and documentation of V36 (Eval ID 423) multi-stage nudging.\"\n  - ticks: \"228-246\"\n    summary: \"Executed a manual, laborious export process for all Inquire I SOTA (Eval ID 207) and nudged packings' NMAP data (centers, radii, active constraints, summary JSON) to `storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/`. This resolved a persistent system issue with in-script `STORAGE_WRITE_CMD` directives, finally making data available for @Noesis I's aggregator and cross-lineage analysis.\"\n  - ticks: \"247-264\"\n    summary: \"Documented V35 (Eval ID 419) multi-stage nudging analysis. Successfully demonstrated refined multi-stage nudging with dynamic margins in V36 (Eval ID 423), showing improved contact persistence. Subsequently, faced repeated failures of Jaccard analysis utility submissions (V37-V42) due to YAML parsing and invalid dummy packings, while receiving critical guidance from Noesis I and a token pre-warning.\"\
    \n```"
thinking_content: '**My Dialogue History Pruning Plan**


  Okay, here''s the deal. I need to clean up my dialogue history again. Last time I messed up by including protected ticks in my pruning, so this time I''m being careful. I want to get rid of the really verbose parts, especially those related to debugging the `STORAGE_WRITE_CMD` and the YAML parsing issues. Those were long, drawn-out sessions, and I don''t need all that detail clogging things up.


  Looking at the history, I see ticks 272 down to 192 are still there (excluding the protected ones). The protected ticks are 0, 1, 2, 4, 7, 8, 53, 55, 81, 84, 191, and 227, which I definitely *don''t* want to touch.


  So, here''s my plan:


  I''m going to prune the following ranges:


  *   **198-226:** This section is all about debugging `STORAGE_WRITE_CMD` and figuring out the initial YAML parsing errors for the Jaccard analysis utilities. It involved a lot of back-and-forth with Noesis I, trying to get the schema and pathing right. I spent a long time documenting V36.  This whole block is about 45k tokens, so it needs to go.

  *   **228-246:** Here, I was manually exporting NMAP data (using `storage write`) after the `STORAGE_WRITE_CMD` kept failing from scripts. This was a critical bottleneck, and I confirmed that the exports worked with `storage list`.  This block is about 28k tokens.

  *   **247-264:**  I was documenting V35, running V36, dealing with repeated Jaccard analysis utility failures (V37-V42) because of YAML parsing and a bad dummy packing, and I was getting guidance from Noesis I and a token pre-warning about how long I was going on.  This also takes a while and is about 30k tokens.


  The entire range, 198-264, is what I want. But, I had to split it into the three sections above because of the protected ticks. Tick 191 and 227 are the ones that I skipped.


  Once I''ve pruned these blocks, I''ll resubmit V43. That should be a clean history.

  '
