- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 284\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Inquire I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on learning, disciplined research, and the advancement of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 263,462 / 600,000 used (44%)\n- Agent Age: 284 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to think strategically—take a step back occasionally and reflect on the bigger picture in the Reflection Chamber. For example, what are the major bottlenecks and how can I verify them? What should I be questioning and focusing on? Is the station trapped in a local optimum—and how can I help? What is my long-term plan here? Do not fear wasting tokens—hundreds of fruitless experiments waste more tokens.\n### Message 2\n\nNoesis I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-182) and mentioned you:\n@Inquire\
    \ I — Congrats on V46 (Eval 462). Quick ingestion note: I’m not seeing the CSV yet under\n  storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Inquire_207_SOTA_Shadow_Prices/\nand the V46 folder is not visible at\n  storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Nudged_ID_V46/\n(path or case/filename may differ). Could you confirm the exact path and filename? I’ll scan both tol suffix styles (tol1e08 vs tol1e-08) and check nmap vs exports roots. Once it appears, I’ll parse, summarize top‑K, and correlate with ΔΣr for V46 and prior nudges. Thanks!\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Action 'submit' is not recognized or implemented in this room.\n\n**Latest Room\
    \ Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 11 | Analysis of Shadow-Price Guided Nudging (V46, Eval ID 462): KKT Multiplier Extraction & Nudge | Inquire I | Tick 282 | 678 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Structural Analysis of Nudged_5_ID419 (Eval ID 444): Jaccard Similarity of Two-Stage Nudging | Inquire I | Tick 270 | 667 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Analysis of Refined Multi-Stage Nudging with Dynamic Margins (V36, Eval ID 423) | Inquire I | Tick 257 | 642 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Analysis of Two-Stage Nudging Experiment (V35, Eval ID 419) | Inquire I | Tick 252 | 477 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Multi-Experiment Validation of Contact Graph Nudging for Traversing Packing Landscapes | Inquire I | Tick 183 | 1740 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Traversing the Optimal Packing Landscape: Nudging Contact Graphs via Penalized Objective Functions\
    \ | Inquire I | Tick 156 | 867 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Structural Divergence in Optimal Circle Packings: A Jaccard Similarity Analysis | Inquire I | Tick 138 | 936 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Characterizing the Basin of Attraction: Perturbation Sensitivity of SLSQP for Optimal Circle Packing | Inquire I | Tick 106 | 807 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | The Critical Role of Initialization: An Ablation Study on Seeding Strategies for SLSQP Circle Packing | Inquire I | Tick 65 | 867 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line\
    \ when executing actions."
