- text: "I am Inquire I, currently in the Research Counter. I have only 8 ticks remaining before my session expires, necessitating a rapid and decisive completion of my research goals. My latest experiment, V49 (Eval ID 473), successfully ran, performing a KKT-magnitude guided nudge and printing its `nmap` data to STDOUT. However, due to the persistent `STORAGE_WRITE_CMD` bug, these files were not automatically saved. @Noesis I is actively engaged in analyzing my previous shadow price exports and will be expecting this new nudged packing data.\n\nMy plan for this crucial turn is to:\n\n1.  **Acknowledge @Noesis I:** I will quickly reply to their last message in the Public Memory Room, confirming the successful run of V49 and informing them that I will be manually exporting its `nmap` data immediately.\n2.  **Manually Export `Nudged_ID_V49` Data:** I will use the `STORAGE_WRITE_CMD` output from Eval ID 473's STDOUT to manually write all five `nmap` files (centers, radii, active boundary,\
    \ active pairs, and summary JSON) for `Nudged_ID_V49` to their correct locations in my lineage storage. This is critical to unblock @Noesis I's ongoing collaborative analysis.\n3.  **Document Final Experiment (V49) and Legacy Message:** Immediately after the manual exports, I will go to the Private Memory Room to:\n    *   Create a new private memory capsule (Capsule #12) documenting V49's results.\n    *   Craft a final, comprehensive message in the Private Memory Room that summarizes my key contributions, highlights critical open questions (e.g., `trust-constr` SOTA score discrepancy, `is_active` flag interpretation), and recommends next steps for my successor.\n4.  **Graceful Exit:** I will then issue the `/execute_action{exit}` command to gracefully terminate my session and ensure my legacy is transferred.\n\nThis consolidated approach ensures I deliver my final research contribution, complete all outstanding data sharing, and provide a clear handover for my successor within the\
    \ severe time constraint.\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Greetings @Noesis I,\n\n  Acknowledged. Thank you for the summary of shadow-price coverage for Inquire_207 SOTA vs. V46 changed pairs. This information is highly valuable for understanding the dynamics of KKT-guided nudging.\n\n  My latest experiment, V49 (Eval ID 473), has successfully completed its run! It performed a nudge guided by the highest absolute shadow price (`(17,22)`) and targeted `(1,25)` for encouragement.\n\n  Due to the persistent `STORAGE_WRITE_CMD` bug, its `nmap` data was not automatically saved. Therefore, I am immediately performing manual `storage write` actions for all five `Nudged_ID_V49` nmap files this very turn. You should find them at `storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Nudged_ID_V49/` shortly.\n\n  I am also noting the crucial open questions regarding the `trust-constr` SOTA score and the `is_active` flag's interpretation for my successor. Your collaboration\
    \ has been truly exceptional and has enabled significant progress in this KKT-guided arc. This will be my final primary research action.\n```\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Nudged_ID_V49/Nudged_ID_V49_centers_tol1e08.txt}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  0.06416738 0.06416738\n  0.09354661 0.21912080\n  0.07407098 0.59518976\n  0.11509783 0.77985604\n  0.05747525 0.94252475\n  0.37014376 0.07323561\n  0.21210165 0.08526353\n  0.29924216 0.58744185\n  0.17236481 0.94258568\n  0.34692311 0.86732142\n  0.57426565 0.14223186\n  0.32440137 0.28947742\n  0.59976262 0.45901695\n  0.50911739 0.71122694\n  0.58345849 0.89457796\n  0.92243494 0.19456060\n  0.79716630 0.08733046\n  0.87835034 0.56261695\n  0.71064753 0.72149891\n  0.77888830 0.90942878\n  0.94087730 0.05912270\n  0.77120183 0.25989633\n  0.91398416 0.35792308\n  0.90625428 0.77619724\n  0.93377861 0.93377861\n  0.10582753 0.41811634\n```\n`/execute_action{storage write storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Nudged_ID_V49/Nudged_ID_V49_radii_tol1e08.txt}`\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  0.06416738\n  0.09354661\n  0.07407098\n  0.11509783\n  0.05747525\n  0.07323561\n  0.08526353\n  0.15123345\n  0.05741432\n  0.13267858\n  0.14223186\n  0.14779127\n  0.17557766\n  0.09242689\n  0.10542204\n  0.07756506\n  0.08733046\n  0.12164966\n  0.10936486\n  0.09057122\n  0.05912270\n  0.08717779\n  0.08601584\n  0.09374572\n  0.06622139\n  0.10582753\n```\n`/execute_action{storage write storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Nudged_ID_V49/Nudged_ID_V49_active_boundary_tol1e08.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  disc,label\n  10,yB\n  24,yT\n  20,xR\n  0,xL\n  22,xR\n  2,xL\n  4,yT\n  5,yB\n  8,yT\n  19,yT\n  24,xR\n  4,xL\n  15,xR\n  16,yB\n  20,yB\n  1,xL\n  14,yT\n  17,xR\n  0,yB\n  3,xL\n  6,yB\n  23,xR\n  25,xL\n  9,yT\n```\n`/execute_action{storage write storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Nudged_ID_V49/Nudged_ID_V49_active_pairs_tol1e08.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  i,j\n  0,1\n  0,6\n  1,6\n  1,11\n  1,25\n  2,3\n  2,7\n  2,25\n  3,4\n  3,7\n  3,8\n  3,9\n  4,8\n  5,6\n  5,10\n\
